WEBVTT

00:00:05.910 --> 00:00:16.650
<i>Along a zigzag the world turns,</i>
<i>I heave out a sigh.</i>

00:00:16.750 --> 00:00:27.670
<i>Someone pauses along the way,</i>
<i>but reality moves on.</i>

00:00:27.900 --> 00:00:33.200
<i>Treat love as love, treat</i>
<i>dreams as dreams.</i>

00:00:33.300 --> 00:00:38.710
<i>It's difficult to say it in earnest.</i>
<i>The times forge ahead, but...</i>

00:00:38.810 --> 00:00:43.620
<i>I want to make you happy...</i>

00:00:43.750 --> 00:00:49.410
<i>I'll do so like I do to</i>
<i>be myself. Yeah!</i>

00:00:49.520 --> 00:00:54.450
<i>I'll make you happy...</i>

00:00:54.560 --> 00:00:59.860
<i>I dedicate all that</i>
<i>I can do to you.</i>

00:00:59.960 --> 00:01:11.180
<i>Along a zigzag the world turns,</i>
<i>I heave out a sigh.</i>

00:01:11.240 --> 00:01:23.420
<i>Someone pauses along the way,</i>
<i>but love doesn't stop for me.</i>

00:01:27.030 --> 00:01:28.990
"Bokuto Station"

00:01:39.870 --> 00:01:41.300
Hey, hey, hey!

00:01:41.410 --> 00:01:43.400
Miyuki! Just the person
I was looking for!

00:01:43.570 --> 00:01:44.410
Huh?

00:01:44.410 --> 00:01:46.080
Shall we?

00:01:46.080 --> 00:01:47.950
W... Well...

00:01:47.950 --> 00:01:49.810
Come on, Come on.

00:01:49.980 --> 00:01:55.880
Cut!

00:01:56.250 --> 00:01:58.850
That's the worst!

00:01:58.960 --> 00:02:01.720
What's the matter with you, Nakajima?!
Can't you put some emotion into it?!

00:02:01.890 --> 00:02:04.620
Come on, Yoriko.
It's not that easy.

00:02:04.800 --> 00:02:07.460
Can't you even put your
arms around Miyuki?!

00:02:07.630 --> 00:02:08.860
Yikes!

00:02:10.800 --> 00:02:13.460
See! This is how you put your arms
around a woman! Is that so hard?!

00:02:13.640 --> 00:02:14.330
D'oh!

00:02:14.570 --> 00:02:15.900
Yoriko...

00:02:16.010 --> 00:02:17.980
...you're asking the
unreasonable.

00:02:18.280 --> 00:02:20.840
What do you mean?! Why
is it so unreasonable?!

00:02:21.180 --> 00:02:25.340
Because... Nakajima has special
feelings for Miyuki.

00:02:25.450 --> 00:02:28.150
And I'm sure he's thought
out exactly how...

00:02:28.250 --> 00:02:30.850
...he'd like to hold her
for the first time.

00:02:31.390 --> 00:02:33.410
If you try to force
them together...

00:02:33.590 --> 00:02:34.390
Aoi?

00:02:34.390 --> 00:02:35.550
Yes?

00:02:35.730 --> 00:02:38.360
You're the one who's forcing
them together.

00:02:42.230 --> 00:02:44.030
Uh... oops.

00:02:44.140 --> 00:02:45.470
Sorry!

00:02:45.640 --> 00:02:46.860
Hey, Yoriko.

00:02:46.970 --> 00:02:50.410
What does this have to
do with traffic safety?

00:02:51.080 --> 00:02:54.530
Kids these days
are very picky.

00:02:54.710 --> 00:02:57.370
It has to be a good play, otherwise
the kids won't even watch.

00:02:58.050 --> 00:02:59.410
Oh!

00:02:59.580 --> 00:03:00.380
Chief!

00:03:00.990 --> 00:03:02.980
If you aren't totally serious
about your performance...

00:03:03.090 --> 00:03:05.280
...you'll be heckled
right off the stage!

00:03:05.460 --> 00:03:07.860
Right. I've heard of an officer whose
acting dreams were murdered...

00:03:07.960 --> 00:03:11.360
...because he was so terrible
and got heckled so much!

00:03:12.160 --> 00:03:15.030
A cop whose acting dreams
were murdered?!

00:03:15.200 --> 00:03:17.830
That poor officer. I wonder
who it was?

00:03:18.000 --> 00:03:18.760
Hmph.

00:03:20.240 --> 00:03:21.230
All right, all right.

00:03:21.340 --> 00:03:23.030
Let's practice, people!

00:03:23.140 --> 00:03:24.570
Practice!

00:03:25.710 --> 00:03:27.140
Hey, Hey, Hey!

00:03:27.250 --> 00:03:29.250
Miyuki! Just the person I was looking for!

00:03:29.250 --> 00:03:30.180
No! That's not it!

00:03:30.180 --> 00:03:30.810
Huh?

00:03:32.520 --> 00:03:33.810
Hey, Hey, Hey!

00:03:33.920 --> 00:03:34.420
Miyuki!

00:03:34.420 --> 00:03:35.610
No!

00:03:35.790 --> 00:03:40.530
Hey, Hey, Hey!

00:03:40.530 --> 00:03:41.180
No!

00:03:41.360 --> 00:03:42.590
Hey!!!!

00:03:42.660 --> 00:03:44.990
No, no no no!
That's not it!

00:03:52.970 --> 00:03:54.130
Let's forget this
for a while...

00:03:54.240 --> 00:03:55.940
...and go straight to your scene, Natsumi.

00:03:55.940 --> 00:03:56.910
Yahoo!

00:03:57.740 --> 00:03:58.670
Stop where
you are!

00:03:58.780 --> 00:04:00.870
You can't get away, you traffic
light-disobeying monster!

00:04:01.410 --> 00:04:02.910
Who? Me?

00:04:02.910 --> 00:04:04.610
Yeah! That's the ticket!

00:04:04.780 --> 00:04:08.150
"Kin-san;" Classic Japanese
television and movie figure.
"Playboy Kin-san"
to the rescue!

00:04:11.860 --> 00:04:13.450
Cut! Cut! Cut!

00:04:14.090 --> 00:04:16.890
How come our combat team leader has
suddenly become "Playboy Kin-san?!"

00:04:17.460 --> 00:04:18.290
Sorry.

00:04:18.460 --> 00:04:22.400
You thought you'd make it as a
cop when you can't even act?!

00:04:22.870 --> 00:04:25.670
Gee, she sure isn't
herself today.

00:04:25.840 --> 00:04:26.770
No kidding.

00:04:26.870 --> 00:04:29.770
I've heard that becoming a director
totally changes your personality.

00:04:29.940 --> 00:04:30.600
Yeah..

00:04:44.990 --> 00:04:46.120
Soldiers...

00:04:46.220 --> 00:04:48.690
They've done it again!

00:04:48.790 --> 00:04:49.560
Take a look at this.

00:04:49.730 --> 00:04:50.660
Ooh!

00:04:50.660 --> 00:04:52.690
"Traffic Safety Week"
Ooh!

00:04:53.260 --> 00:04:55.700
What stupidity.

00:04:55.800 --> 00:04:58.890
They haven't even established their
identities as superheroes.

00:04:59.000 --> 00:05:01.490
That means they don't
have a purpose.

00:05:01.610 --> 00:05:03.010
This is a travesty!

00:05:03.170 --> 00:05:03.660
Yeah!

00:05:04.280 --> 00:05:06.240
Are we ninjas going
to stand for this?!

00:05:06.610 --> 00:05:08.010
No! Never!

00:05:08.010 --> 00:05:08.850
That's right!

00:05:08.850 --> 00:05:09.240
We won't!

00:05:09.310 --> 00:05:09.350
We can't!

00:05:09.350 --> 00:05:10.940
We won't!

00:05:11.120 --> 00:05:14.210
And what measures should we
take against these people?

00:05:14.790 --> 00:05:16.750
Resolute Education!
Resolute Guidance!

00:05:16.920 --> 00:05:18.180
That's right.

00:05:18.290 --> 00:05:21.290
"Burajaa:" A pun on 'Brother' and 'Brassiere'
We, the Black Brothers of Sumida,
must educate and train these...

00:05:21.290 --> 00:05:24.750
...so-called superheroes in
proper heroic etiquette!

00:05:24.860 --> 00:05:25.690
Starting tomorrow.

00:05:27.030 --> 00:05:32.400
Hail Black Brothers!

00:05:32.600 --> 00:05:37.540
FILE. 20
FIGHT! TRAFFIC
COMBAT TEAM OB3!

00:05:37.780 --> 00:05:42.010
"Traffic Safety Theater"

00:05:44.520 --> 00:05:47.380
Lalala!

00:05:47.620 --> 00:05:49.590
"National Traffic Safety Week"
This is exciting!

00:05:52.290 --> 00:05:54.050
Hey, hey, hey!

00:05:54.160 --> 00:05:54.750
Miyuki!

00:05:55.230 --> 00:05:56.190
Huh?

00:05:58.100 --> 00:06:01.900
<i>Wow! Kobayakawa</i>
<i>in that skirt...</i>

00:06:02.000 --> 00:06:03.590
<i>That skirt!</i>

00:06:04.770 --> 00:06:06.460
<i>Oh my!</i>

00:06:06.640 --> 00:06:08.070
Ow!

00:06:08.540 --> 00:06:09.800
What do you think
you're doing?!

00:06:09.970 --> 00:06:13.030
Hurry up and say
your next line!

00:06:13.880 --> 00:06:16.540
All right. Green
means go.

00:06:16.650 --> 00:06:18.810
Yellow means hurry
and go for it.

00:06:18.920 --> 00:06:21.440
And red means go if you
can get away with it.

00:06:21.550 --> 00:06:23.850
Now hurry and run along.

00:06:23.850 --> 00:06:24.390
How come?!

00:06:24.390 --> 00:06:25.220
Huh?

00:06:25.220 --> 00:06:26.520
Yeah, the light's still red...

00:06:26.620 --> 00:06:28.960
...so how's she supposed
to cross?

00:06:29.130 --> 00:06:30.490
Where's she hurrying
off to?

00:06:31.000 --> 00:06:34.430
Where?! Well, that's
difficult... right?

00:06:34.600 --> 00:06:35.590
Yeah.

00:06:35.770 --> 00:06:38.670
Oh! You won't
tell us!

00:06:38.770 --> 00:06:41.030
It's got to be a
secret place!

00:06:41.610 --> 00:06:45.040
So where is it? Where's
the secret place?

00:06:48.210 --> 00:06:50.270
You love
each other!

00:06:50.380 --> 00:06:52.320
You love each other!
Go for it! Go for it!

00:06:52.480 --> 00:06:53.540
Ugh.

00:06:53.720 --> 00:06:56.650
Miyuki and Nakajima
are dying out there.

00:06:56.820 --> 00:07:01.380
How embarrassing. Being heckled by
a bunch of little kindergarten kids.

00:07:01.660 --> 00:07:05.600
Let's skip over the next 10 or 20 lines,
and go straight to our part!

00:07:05.760 --> 00:07:06.130
Yeah!

00:07:07.330 --> 00:07:08.490
Stop right where
you are!

00:07:09.330 --> 00:07:12.100
You light running tempter
of children!

00:07:12.270 --> 00:07:15.000
Even if a traffic judge
were to let you off...

00:07:15.170 --> 00:07:17.540
...we, the Traffic Combat Team OB3s,
won't show you any mercy!

00:07:17.710 --> 00:07:20.510
Yeah!
She's cool!

00:07:21.310 --> 00:07:23.580
And that!

00:07:24.280 --> 00:07:26.150
The monster and the heroes
don't know how to act!

00:07:26.250 --> 00:07:28.410
I don't feel any passion!

00:07:28.750 --> 00:07:30.520
You guys are boring!

00:07:31.020 --> 00:07:32.550
Aah! She got me!

00:07:33.060 --> 00:07:35.750
I'll remember you,
you OB3s!

00:07:37.160 --> 00:07:39.430
Good always wins
in the end.

00:07:39.530 --> 00:07:40.550
So remember
everyone...

00:07:40.660 --> 00:07:43.260
...never go through
a red light...

00:07:48.810 --> 00:07:51.330
Hey! Are you kids paying
attention here?!

00:07:51.940 --> 00:07:54.500
Hmpf! But it's boring!

00:07:54.680 --> 00:07:58.770
I dunno, but it doesn't seem
like you're into it!

00:07:59.980 --> 00:08:01.540
Why you bratty
little!

00:08:01.720 --> 00:08:03.350
Natsumi! Don't!

00:08:03.520 --> 00:08:04.850
Let go of me,
Miyuki!

00:08:04.960 --> 00:08:07.290
"Doesn't seem like we're
into it," huh?!

00:08:07.390 --> 00:08:10.290
Well how're you supposed to get the point
when you're not even watching us?!

00:08:10.460 --> 00:08:12.590
And that's the end of this
morning's show.

00:08:12.760 --> 00:08:15.600
Everybody come back here after
you've had your lunch!

00:08:19.040 --> 00:08:21.440
What an inept
performance!

00:08:21.540 --> 00:08:26.500
How are kids supposed to stay interested
when the act is that lame?

00:08:27.810 --> 00:08:30.510
Brothers! We'll
use plan D-3!

00:08:30.680 --> 00:08:32.650
P... Plan D-3?!

00:08:32.750 --> 00:08:35.650
Isn't that a little too
dangerous?

00:08:39.420 --> 00:08:42.650
"Changing Room"
Brats! The nerve of
those little imps!

00:08:42.760 --> 00:08:44.020
Making fun of us!

00:08:44.200 --> 00:08:45.920
Don't let 'em get
to you, Natsumi.

00:08:46.030 --> 00:08:47.730
I don't think they meant
it maliciously.

00:08:47.830 --> 00:08:51.130
The fact that they said something
shows that they were watching.

00:08:51.600 --> 00:08:53.130
That's true,
but still...

00:08:53.640 --> 00:08:56.200
Kindergarten kids
these days...

00:08:56.310 --> 00:08:58.370
They're so
cynical...

00:08:58.740 --> 00:09:01.370
You've got a
point there.

00:09:01.810 --> 00:09:04.780
<i>Good! They've taken</i>
<i>off their costumes!</i>

00:09:13.020 --> 00:09:15.750
Hey, cute panties,
Natsumi!

00:09:16.360 --> 00:09:19.260
Why, thank you, Miss Yoriko.
What refined taste you have.

00:09:20.160 --> 00:09:21.890
Pan... panties?!

00:09:22.070 --> 00:09:23.930
Look! See how nice
they fit right there!

00:09:24.030 --> 00:09:26.800
It makes your bum
look really sexy!

00:09:26.970 --> 00:09:28.130
S... Sexy?!

00:09:41.590 --> 00:09:43.990
<i>Get a grip. Get a grip.</i>

00:09:51.330 --> 00:09:54.200
Miyuki, your boobs have gotten bigger.

00:09:54.200 --> 00:09:55.930
What do you think you're doing, Yoriko?!

00:09:56.100 --> 00:09:57.970
I'm just feeling it...

00:09:58.070 --> 00:10:00.370
...then I'll tell Nakajima all about it.

00:10:00.370 --> 00:10:01.960
Yoriko!

00:10:02.070 --> 00:10:02.670
Give it back!

00:10:02.670 --> 00:10:05.470
Give it back!
Ow! Don't pinch! That hurts!

00:10:05.580 --> 00:10:06.910
What's wrong with a little touch?!

00:10:06.910 --> 00:10:08.570
What do you mean..."little touch?!"

00:10:08.680 --> 00:10:10.010
You don't go around feeling
another woman's breasts.

00:10:10.180 --> 00:10:10.940
<i>Don't be silly.</i>

00:10:11.050 --> 00:10:14.250
<i>I'm Umihiko Yamakawa, ninja</i>
<i>straight and narrow.</i>

00:10:14.350 --> 00:10:15.680
<i>I have a duty</i>
<i>to carry out.</i>

00:10:17.420 --> 00:10:18.910
<i>But what's wrong with</i>
<i>just a little peek?</i>

00:10:19.020 --> 00:10:22.250
<i>No, no! But I can't</i>
<i>help myself!</i>

00:10:22.360 --> 00:10:25.660
<i>Even a little peek?</i>
<i>No, I can't!</i>

00:10:27.630 --> 00:10:28.530
<i>Oh, I know...</i>

00:10:28.630 --> 00:10:31.600
<i>... perhaps there's a need</i>
<i>to evaluate the subjects.</i>

00:10:36.040 --> 00:10:37.840
<i>Wow!</i>

00:10:45.450 --> 00:10:47.440
<i>Boxers?!</i>

00:10:47.620 --> 00:10:49.590
Hmm?

00:10:51.760 --> 00:10:53.590
<i>Those damn OB3s!</i>

00:10:53.760 --> 00:10:58.390
<i>How dare they pull something like this</i>
<i>on me after getting me so aroused!</i>

00:11:06.740 --> 00:11:08.860
Hey, Hey, Hey, Miyuki...

00:11:08.970 --> 00:11:11.030
...if you want to get
across faster...

00:11:11.140 --> 00:11:15.940
...it's better to wait as close
as possible to the traffic.

00:11:16.110 --> 00:11:18.880
What? But that'd be
really dangerous.

00:11:19.950 --> 00:11:23.610
Hmm... Seems a lot less stiff
than it did this morning.

00:11:23.790 --> 00:11:24.690
I agree.

00:11:24.860 --> 00:11:26.410
Come on. Go ahead!

00:11:26.590 --> 00:11:29.290
But... no, it's too
dangerous.

00:11:29.460 --> 00:11:32.330
No problem! Hurry
up and cross!

00:11:32.500 --> 00:11:33.430
Stop right there!

00:11:33.430 --> 00:11:34.450
Who's that?

00:11:34.630 --> 00:11:38.630
Stop, light-running seducer of
traffic rule-obeying little girls!

00:11:38.800 --> 00:11:41.600
Even if a traffic court
judge lets you off...

00:11:41.770 --> 00:11:44.100
...the OB3 Traffic Combat Team
will show you no mercy!

00:11:44.280 --> 00:11:45.000
OB Red!

00:11:45.180 --> 00:11:45.940
OB Blue!

00:11:46.110 --> 00:11:46.910
OB Purple!

00:11:47.180 --> 00:11:48.770
It really is pretty bad.

00:11:48.950 --> 00:11:52.610
What's so great about a bunch of
superheroes just showing up?

00:11:53.120 --> 00:11:55.880
Together, we
are the OB3!

00:11:57.150 --> 00:12:04.320
Hey! Neato! That
was cool!

00:12:04.700 --> 00:12:05.920
What was that?

00:12:06.100 --> 00:12:09.830
Miyuki, if you use smoke bombs, how
about a little warning beforehand?

00:12:10.330 --> 00:12:12.560
Huh? But I didn't
do that.

00:12:15.810 --> 00:12:18.070
We sure surprised them.

00:12:19.110 --> 00:12:20.440
To carry out
plan D-3...

00:12:20.540 --> 00:12:22.770
...we will use any technique,
even smoke bombs.

00:12:22.880 --> 00:12:25.080
We will stop
at nothing!

00:12:25.780 --> 00:12:29.550
But, that's it for the
fun and games.

00:12:30.120 --> 00:12:31.050
Brother Yamakawa!

00:12:32.120 --> 00:12:36.120
Ha! Now for double
the fun!

00:12:38.100 --> 00:12:40.360
My brothers, you will see
I have a distinct style.

00:12:43.400 --> 00:12:45.770
You see that? Natsumi and her
friends are really pretty good!

00:12:45.940 --> 00:12:46.730
Yeah!

00:12:46.900 --> 00:12:48.440
Huh?

00:12:50.710 --> 00:12:54.670
We are the Black Brothers
of Sumida.

00:12:54.780 --> 00:12:56.450
Hey you, Traffic Light-Running Monster!

00:12:56.450 --> 00:12:58.180
Huh?!

00:12:58.280 --> 00:12:59.280
Who... me?

00:12:59.280 --> 00:13:00.480
Fear not.

00:13:00.580 --> 00:13:02.550
Now that I, General Winker,
have arrived...

00:13:02.650 --> 00:13:04.750
...we will end the tyranny
of the OB3.

00:13:05.560 --> 00:13:08.080
First, we will kidnap
all the children.

00:13:08.260 --> 00:13:08.780
Do it!

00:13:10.290 --> 00:13:12.560
Wow!

00:13:12.730 --> 00:13:13.660
This is neat!

00:13:13.760 --> 00:13:16.230
We're part of the
play, too!

00:13:16.400 --> 00:13:20.460
Natsumi and those guys have
finally smartened up.

00:13:20.640 --> 00:13:22.000
Come on everyone! You
know what to do!

00:13:22.340 --> 00:13:23.900
Help us!

00:13:24.010 --> 00:13:25.980
OB3!

00:13:27.540 --> 00:13:28.740
Yoriko...

00:13:28.910 --> 00:13:32.280
...why are these guys here?
Were they in the script?

00:13:32.450 --> 00:13:33.250
No!

00:13:33.420 --> 00:13:35.180
Then who in the
world are they?

00:13:35.350 --> 00:13:38.580
Maybe the Chief got them to show
up, just to jazz up our play a bit.

00:13:38.760 --> 00:13:40.950
You mean he brought them in,
but kept it a secret from us?

00:13:41.130 --> 00:13:43.420
I get it. That makes
sense.

00:13:43.590 --> 00:13:45.530
Hello! How's
it going?

00:13:45.700 --> 00:13:46.750
Chief!

00:13:47.400 --> 00:13:49.730
This year's play seems to
be quite the production.

00:13:49.830 --> 00:13:51.960
But, good job.
Keep it up.

00:13:52.070 --> 00:13:54.970
Good luck.

00:13:55.510 --> 00:13:57.370
Oh...

00:13:57.540 --> 00:13:59.670
<i>Hmm... Seeing them</i>
<i>gives me hope...</i>

00:13:59.780 --> 00:14:03.010
<i>... that my murdered acting</i>
<i>dreams may sprout anew.</i>

00:14:03.780 --> 00:14:05.040
So it wasn't him,
after all.

00:14:05.220 --> 00:14:06.740
Then what's that old
geezer doing here?

00:14:09.220 --> 00:14:11.350
If you are worried about the
safety of the children...

00:14:11.460 --> 00:14:14.220
...then you must do as
I, General Winker, say.

00:14:14.930 --> 00:14:16.760
Miyuki, what should
we do?

00:14:16.860 --> 00:14:17.990
Shall I call for
back-up?

00:14:18.160 --> 00:14:20.890
Wait! Don't
call yet!

00:14:21.000 --> 00:14:22.900
There are too many hostages
to risk anything.

00:14:23.570 --> 00:14:25.230
You, Traffic Light-Running Monster!

00:14:25.340 --> 00:14:27.270
Attack OB3!

00:14:27.440 --> 00:14:29.960
What? A... Attack?

00:14:30.240 --> 00:14:34.040
If you do not
obey, then...

00:14:34.210 --> 00:14:35.610
Waah!

00:14:35.710 --> 00:14:37.870
I'm scared! Ooh,
I'm so scared!

00:14:38.520 --> 00:14:40.880
So, Traffic Light-Running Monster...

00:14:40.980 --> 00:14:43.610
...go ahead and
attack the OB3.

00:14:43.790 --> 00:14:46.280
Who the heck are you
guys, anyway?

00:14:46.460 --> 00:14:49.260
We are the Black Brothers
of Sumida.

00:14:49.430 --> 00:14:52.950
The "Black Brothers of Sumida?"
And what's your purpose?

00:14:53.130 --> 00:14:55.290
The first principle
of evil...

00:14:55.400 --> 00:14:59.100
...is to fight against the
defenders of justice.

00:14:59.700 --> 00:15:01.670
Huh?!

00:15:04.610 --> 00:15:06.540
Wonder what Nakajima's
saying to them?

00:15:06.710 --> 00:15:09.980
He's getting them to explain
themselves! What else?

00:15:10.150 --> 00:15:11.170
I wonder.

00:15:11.350 --> 00:15:12.650
I see!

00:15:12.820 --> 00:15:15.220
All right, Traffic Light-Running
Monster! Attack!

00:15:15.390 --> 00:15:16.910
Okay!

00:15:17.390 --> 00:15:18.980
O... Okay?!

00:15:19.090 --> 00:15:20.090
Now we're in trouble!

00:15:20.090 --> 00:15:21.180
Now we're in trouble!
OB Red!

00:15:21.360 --> 00:15:23.220
Take this!

00:15:28.370 --> 00:15:29.890
Wow!

00:15:31.030 --> 00:15:32.020
What's that?

00:15:32.200 --> 00:15:36.100
They must have put smoke bombs on
our costumes when we changed!

00:15:36.270 --> 00:15:38.040
Oh, no! On
mine, too?!

00:15:38.140 --> 00:15:40.130
I'll get them
for this!

00:15:40.310 --> 00:15:42.140
Wait, Natsumi!

00:15:42.710 --> 00:15:43.740
What is it, Aoi?

00:15:44.480 --> 00:15:48.110
They might have other smoke
bombs in the audience, too.

00:15:48.290 --> 00:15:51.250
Aoi, don't talk like that, you're
starting to scare me!

00:15:51.890 --> 00:15:53.550
Well, what are we
supposed to do?

00:15:55.590 --> 00:15:58.690
Good shot!
This is fun!

00:15:58.860 --> 00:16:01.420
Go get him, Natsumi!

00:16:01.700 --> 00:16:03.670
Tsu... Tsujimoto!

00:16:06.400 --> 00:16:08.230
This is enough, don't
you think?

00:16:08.410 --> 00:16:10.310
Take a look at their faces.

00:16:10.310 --> 00:16:10.710
Huh?

00:16:10.870 --> 00:16:13.170
Yeah!
Go!

00:16:13.880 --> 00:16:15.570
The second principle
of evil is...

00:16:15.680 --> 00:16:19.170
...never show mercy to the
defenders of justice.

00:16:22.620 --> 00:16:23.710
Ouch!

00:16:23.890 --> 00:16:27.050
Natsumi, get them to set off
a few more smoke bombs.

00:16:27.220 --> 00:16:28.280
What?!

00:16:28.460 --> 00:16:31.920
They've got to be setting off those
bombs using a remote control.

00:16:32.030 --> 00:16:34.660
If I find out what frequency they're using,
I should be able to stop them!

00:16:34.830 --> 00:16:36.300
Aha! Nice thinking,
Miyuki!

00:16:36.470 --> 00:16:37.800
Oh, my!

00:16:37.970 --> 00:16:39.300
Prepare to meet your
demise, OB3s!

00:16:39.470 --> 00:16:40.340
Huh?

00:16:40.340 --> 00:16:42.200
First I'll destroy you...

00:16:42.370 --> 00:16:48.440
...then I'm gonna break all the traffic rules
and cause lots and lots of accidents!

00:16:54.250 --> 00:16:56.150
Come on, Nakajima.

00:16:56.320 --> 00:16:58.050
My name's not
Nakajima.

00:16:58.160 --> 00:17:00.680
I'm the Traffic Light-
Running Monster!

00:17:01.120 --> 00:17:03.020
Calm down!

00:17:03.130 --> 00:17:03.890
Let's talk about this.

00:17:04.060 --> 00:17:06.760
I don't want to
be bombed!

00:17:06.930 --> 00:17:08.590
Take this!

00:17:13.140 --> 00:17:16.040
Traffic Light-Running
Monster, go get 'em!

00:17:22.780 --> 00:17:23.580
Got it!

00:17:23.680 --> 00:17:25.650
Transmitting counter-
signal. Go!

00:17:27.380 --> 00:17:29.820
Great! That'll put an end
to their smoke show!

00:17:31.760 --> 00:17:34.320
Nakajima's gone
too far this time.

00:17:34.490 --> 00:17:37.360
I can't move!

00:17:39.400 --> 00:17:41.630
Take a good look,
children!

00:17:41.730 --> 00:17:44.200
Monsters are strong
and beautiful!

00:17:44.300 --> 00:17:46.530
Until you are strong enough
to fight against evil...

00:17:46.640 --> 00:17:52.080
...you can't say that "Justice
will always prevail!"

00:17:52.780 --> 00:17:53.800
Go get him,
Natsumi!

00:17:53.980 --> 00:17:55.070
Yoriko, don't
give up!

00:17:55.180 --> 00:17:56.200
Aoi! It's not
over yet!

00:17:56.380 --> 00:17:58.250
Go catch those
bad guys!

00:17:58.420 --> 00:18:07.220
Go, Go, OB3!

00:18:08.390 --> 00:18:09.390
Kids!

00:18:09.390 --> 00:18:09.560
<i>Traffic violations are unforgivable... unacceptable.</i>

00:18:09.560 --> 00:18:10.630
Natsumi!

00:18:10.630 --> 00:18:14.960
<i>Traffic violations are unforgivable... unacceptable.</i>

00:18:15.200 --> 00:18:16.630
<i>The minions of dark evils are</i>
<i>violating traffic lights.</i>

00:18:16.630 --> 00:18:17.970
It's just about time...

00:18:17.970 --> 00:18:18.200
<i>The minions of dark evils are</i>
<i>violating traffic lights.</i>

00:18:18.200 --> 00:18:21.360
...for the third principle of evil...

00:18:21.540 --> 00:18:22.210
Traffic Light-Running Monster!

00:18:22.210 --> 00:18:23.740
<i>The easy trap is looking forthe chance..</i>

00:18:23.740 --> 00:18:27.210
We can't lose with their
cheers behind us!

00:18:27.210 --> 00:18:27.770
<i>The easy trap is looking forthe chance...</i>

00:18:28.210 --> 00:18:28.310
<i>... to destroy the peace of this town.</i>

00:18:28.310 --> 00:18:32.320
OB Blue's ultimate weapon! The
Superduper Roundhouse Kick!

00:18:32.320 --> 00:18:32.450
<i>... to destroy the peace of this town.</i>

00:18:32.450 --> 00:18:34.220
The Superduper Roundhouse
Kick?! No way!

00:18:34.220 --> 00:18:34.450
<i>... to destroy the peace of this town.</i>

00:18:35.990 --> 00:18:39.790
<i>Now let's have courage burned in our hearts.</i>

00:18:39.790 --> 00:18:42.660
Cool! How'd she do that?!
I wanna be like her!

00:18:42.790 --> 00:18:43.290
<i>Red, stop! Blue, go!</i>

00:18:43.290 --> 00:18:45.730
Next, how about OB Purple's special weapon?

00:18:45.730 --> 00:18:45.890
<i>Red, stop! Blue, go!</i>

00:18:46.000 --> 00:18:46.800
<i>Rules must be obeyed!</i>

00:18:46.800 --> 00:18:50.700
Purple Gorgeous Flash Body Attack!

00:18:50.700 --> 00:18:53.930
<i>Rules must be obeyed!</i>

00:18:54.040 --> 00:18:55.010
<i>Allies ofJustice...</i>

00:18:55.010 --> 00:18:57.370
If you resist any further,
the children will be...

00:18:57.370 --> 00:18:59.410
<i>Invincible heroes...</i>

00:18:59.410 --> 00:19:00.610
Go, Go, OB3! Catch those bad guys!

00:19:00.610 --> 00:19:03.310
<i>Sure-Death Transformation!</i>

00:19:03.310 --> 00:19:03.410
Go, Go, OB3! Catch those bad guys!

00:19:03.410 --> 00:19:06.810
<i>Go for it, Hurricane Attack!</i>

00:19:06.810 --> 00:19:06.920
Go, Go, OB3! Catch those bad guys!

00:19:06.920 --> 00:19:10.010
<i>Slow down, buddy!</i>

00:19:10.010 --> 00:19:10.120
Go, Go, OB3! Catch those bad guys!

00:19:10.120 --> 00:19:10.920
<i>Can't stand it anymore!</i>

00:19:10.920 --> 00:19:12.920
OB3 Sure-Death Ultimate
Combination Technique!

00:19:12.920 --> 00:19:13.350
<i>Can't stand it anymore!</i>

00:19:13.360 --> 00:19:13.460
Again?!

00:19:13.460 --> 00:19:14.730
<i>Go! Go!</i>

00:19:14.730 --> 00:19:19.250
Vacuum...

00:19:19.250 --> 00:19:19.260
<i>Go! Go!</i>

00:19:19.430 --> 00:19:21.590
Hurricane...

00:19:23.030 --> 00:19:24.630
Attack!

00:19:30.840 --> 00:19:32.710
Hear me, OB3!

00:19:32.810 --> 00:19:35.040
We haven't
lost yet!

00:19:35.150 --> 00:19:39.170
If any of those kids out there break
the traffic rules, even just a little...

00:19:39.280 --> 00:19:42.310
...then you'll know that
we're close by.

00:19:45.620 --> 00:19:48.350
I'm not gonna break
the traffic rules!

00:19:48.530 --> 00:19:50.050
I'm gonna wait
for the light!

00:19:50.230 --> 00:19:53.290
I'm gonna raise my arm when
I cross at the crosswalk!

00:19:53.560 --> 00:19:56.120
We'll obey the
traffic rules!

00:19:56.230 --> 00:19:58.500
We'll watch out for cars!

00:19:58.600 --> 00:20:02.370
We'll raise our arms when we
cross at the crosswalk!

00:20:03.140 --> 00:20:06.470
So you see, I didn't
betray you!

00:20:06.640 --> 00:20:09.700
Well, you sure could
have fooled me!

00:20:09.880 --> 00:20:13.280
But, if Nakajima had
not done that...

00:20:13.380 --> 00:20:16.250
...the kids wouldn't have
watched the play at all.

00:20:17.890 --> 00:20:19.580
That guy was right.

00:20:19.690 --> 00:20:24.150
Superheroes teach children
about justice.

00:20:24.260 --> 00:20:27.060
But that alone
isn't enough.

00:20:27.230 --> 00:20:29.370
What else do you need?

00:20:29.370 --> 00:20:31.430
Monsters.

00:20:31.600 --> 00:20:35.730
There must always be evil
for justice to prevail.

00:20:35.910 --> 00:20:36.800
What?

00:20:36.970 --> 00:20:41.100
People need evil to despise. In other
words, I think that when...

00:20:41.210 --> 00:20:43.240
...people see the bad
guy in action...

00:20:43.350 --> 00:20:46.110
...it makes them want
to believe in justice.

00:20:46.280 --> 00:20:47.440
I get it.

00:20:47.620 --> 00:20:49.180
Yeah! That's
it exactly!

00:20:49.820 --> 00:20:51.480
A half-baked monster
like me...

00:20:51.590 --> 00:20:54.650
...won't make an impression
on the kids.

00:20:54.760 --> 00:20:55.820
That's what
he told me.

00:20:55.990 --> 00:20:56.820
Yeah, so?

00:20:56.990 --> 00:21:02.090
If they hadn't shown up, the kids wouldn't
have promised to obey the traffic laws.

00:21:02.270 --> 00:21:03.400
Hmm.

00:21:03.400 --> 00:21:04.330
Hmm.
Yeah.

00:21:04.730 --> 00:21:06.900
When he told me that,
I was so excited.

00:21:07.000 --> 00:21:09.800
I knew exactly what
I had to do!

00:21:11.810 --> 00:21:14.870
Who were those
guys, anyway?

00:21:15.050 --> 00:21:17.450
The Black Brothers
of Sumida.

00:21:17.610 --> 00:21:20.140
I think we'd better
check them out.

00:21:20.320 --> 00:21:24.010
Let's find out if they'll help us again
with our traffic safety campaign!

00:21:24.120 --> 00:21:26.050
We'll get them to help us. Maybe
we should rewrite the script...

00:21:26.160 --> 00:21:28.720
...and maybe we can get some
bazookas and stuff!

00:21:28.860 --> 00:21:30.490
Yoriko!

00:21:30.660 --> 00:21:35.360
We'll have to give them a hard time
about the smoke bombs, though.

00:21:35.800 --> 00:21:36.860
Huh?

00:21:37.030 --> 00:21:40.370
Just a little bit.
Just a little bit.

00:21:42.340 --> 00:21:44.830
Let's do it, OB3!

00:21:45.010 --> 00:21:46.980
Yeah!

00:22:07.900 --> 00:22:13.470
<i>I live my life my own way, doing</i>
<i>things others wouldn't.</i>

00:22:13.740 --> 00:22:22.080
<i>Being strong isn't enough.</i>
<i>It makes me Ionely.</i>

00:22:24.780 --> 00:22:33.090
<i>I can feel your presence</i>
<i>as if you're right here...</i>

00:22:33.620 --> 00:22:41.190
<i>... but I can't say a word.</i>

00:22:42.670 --> 00:22:49.930
<i>The feelings I hide within might</i>
<i>break into pieces...</i>

00:22:51.470 --> 00:22:58.850
<i>But if I don't say anything,</i>
<i>nothing can begin.</i>

00:22:59.180 --> 00:23:06.410
<i>The wind gently blows...</i>
<i>Time flows...</i>

00:23:06.590 --> 00:23:16.130
<i>Time flows... And soon</i>
<i>I can be honest...</i>

00:23:16.270 --> 00:23:18.890
<i>Thank you,</i>
<i>friend!</i>

00:23:25.440 --> 00:23:27.380
"Handle With Care"

00:23:28.780 --> 00:23:30.800
Rule #1 for Bank Robbery Victims;
You should never resist.

00:23:30.980 --> 00:23:32.450
Rule #1 for Bank Robbers;
Speed is of the essence.

00:23:32.620 --> 00:23:34.140
Rule #2; Press the alarm
button ASAP.

00:23:34.320 --> 00:23:35.580
Rule #2; Don't give them
a chance to move.

00:23:35.750 --> 00:23:37.620
Rule #3; After the robbers
leave, act quickly.

00:23:37.790 --> 00:23:39.550
Rule #3; Don't get greedy.
Get in and get out.

00:23:39.660 --> 00:23:43.420
By the way... 1 million bills weigh 110 grams,
so I can carry at least... 10 billion.

00:23:43.590 --> 00:23:46.190
Are we the best pair of bank
robbers in history?

00:23:47.460 --> 00:23:50.970
Next time on You're Under Arrest, File 21,
"The Bank Robbery Task Force Manual."

00:23:51.100 --> 00:23:53.100
This is a hold up!
